<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Doria family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Doria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Doria were one of the great noble families of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, prominent from the 12th century. Doria admirals won victories over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> at Meloria in 1284 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> at Curzola in 1298, and the family held lands in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>. Its most famous member, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrea-doria">Andrea Doria</a>, reshaped Genoa as an ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1528.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/doria-family.jpg" alt="Doria family" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Facquis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_the_House_of_Doria.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
